/surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name><name><surname>Riis</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Different effects of CSA and CSB deficiency on sensitivity to oxidative DNA damage.</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biol</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>7941</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15340056</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000266-DErrico1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>D'Errico</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Parlanti</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Teson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Degan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lemma</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>The role of CSA in the response to oxidative DNA damage in human cells.</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>4336</fpage><lpage>43</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17297471</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000266-Ishibashi1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ishibashi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayakawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Sekiguchi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>A novel mechanism for preventing mutations caused by oxidation of guanine nucleotides.</article-title><source>EMBO Rep</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>479</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12717453</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000266-Sakumi1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sakumi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Furuichi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsuzuki</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kakuma</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawabata</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Cloning and expression of cDNA for a human enzyme that hydrolyzes 8-oxo- dGTP, a mutagenic substrate for DNA synthesis.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>268</volume><fpage>23524</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8226881</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000266-Fujikawa1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fujikawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamiya</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Yakushiji</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakabeppu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>The oxidized forms of dATP are substrates for the human MutT homologue, the hMTH1 protein.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>274</volume><fpage>18201</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10373420</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000266-Hayakawa1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hayakawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hofer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Thelander</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kitajima</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cai</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Metabolic fate of oxidized guanine ribonucleotides in mammalian cells.</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><volume>38</volume><fpage>3610</fpage><lpage>4</lp